WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.140
A brand-new poster for the upcoming Wonder
Woman 1984 hit the internet earlier this week,

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.440
posted to Twitter by none other than director
Patty Jenkins herself.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.380
We can't blame Jenkins for wanting the world
to see the dazzling poster as soon as possible.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.540
In a word, it's retro.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.279
The one-sheet flawlessly captures the aesthetic
of the 1980s, bursting with every shade of

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.740
the neon rainbow that all come together to
form a massive W.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.760
But it's much more than just an ultra-cool-looking
piece of promotional material.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.900
This Wonder Woman 1984 poster gives fans their
first look at Diana Prince's brand-new costume,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.040
which looks a whole lot like her Gold Armor
from the DC comics.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.020
In the source material, Diana obtains enhanced
abilities when she dons the glimmering get-up:

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:48.591
she's able to fly; withstand explosions, bullets,
energy blasts, and physical attacks; and can

00:00:48.591 --> 00:00:52.670
utilize the retractable faceplate on her helmet
to breathe from a protected air supply if

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.800
her oxygen is low or if the air around her
is unclean.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.800
That should come in handy next time she has
to breathe the air in London.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.860
"Welcome to jolly ol' London."

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:02.950
"It's hideous."

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.200
"Yeah, it's not for everybody."

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:11.120
In DC Comics canon, the Themysciran artisan
Pallas created the Gold Armor and gifted it

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.480
to Diana for use in battles against incredibly
powerful opponents.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.680
It proved its worth in Wonder Woman's fights
against villains like the living weapon Devastation.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.840
Given that Wonder Woman 1984 sees the titular
heroine face off with the Barbara Ann Minerva

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:29.979
iteration of Cheetah, played by Kristen Wiig,
it makes sense why she would need new armor:

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:33.520
she's as formidable a foe as Diana has ever
gone up against before.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.119
A British archaeologist and wealthy heiress,
Barbara transformed into her super-villain

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:42.749
alter-ego after traveling to Africa to visit
a tribe led by a woman with all the force,

00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:44.600
strength, and agility of a cheetah.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.100
When marauders kill the woman, a priest named
Chuma carries out the conference of powers

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.080
from the slain leader to Barbara.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.800
The ceremony comes with severe consequences,
though, as Barbara doesn't meet all the requirements

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.940
to be the perfect host for the Cheetah entity.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:03.420
As a human, she's overcome with pain; as Cheetah,
she's vicious, vile, and bloodthirsty.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.680
"What do you want, Cheetah?"

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.300
"To hurt you, Diana.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.340
What else?"

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.100
We don't yet know how Wonder Woman will cross
paths with Cheetah, but once she does, there's

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:18.480
a strong chance that their first fight could
leave the Amazonian warrior shaken.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.700
She might make a quick trip to Themyscira
and seek the aid of Pallas, who could outfit

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.160
her with the Gold Armor to help ensure a win
over Cheetah in their next battle.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.680
This isn't the only Wonder Woman 1984 media
that fans got a glimpse of this week.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.180
The Spanish-language fan account DC Universe
shared another one-sheet for the sequel as

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.830
displayed at the 2019 Licensing Expo currently
taking place in Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:44.580
Though the Licensing Expo poster is certainly
a visual treat, it doesn't reveal much in

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.660
the way of plot.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:51.000
Warner Bros. and DC Films have stayed incredibly
tight-lipped about the long-awaited Wonder

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:54.970
Woman sequel, revealing very little about
what adventures the eponymous heroine will

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.720
embark on for her second turn on the silver
screen.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.760
All we truly know about Wonder Woman 1984
is its time setting, its villain, and that

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.360
Pedro Pascal will appear as a mysterious and
yet-unnamed politician character.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.360
Chris Pine will also return as pilot Steve
Trevor…somehow.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.640
As for what the movie will be about, it's
said to follow Diana experiencing conflict

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:19.630
with the Soviet Union during the Cold War
before going head-to-head with Cheetah, but

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.940
there's no intel on how everything unfolds.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:25.800
As backward as it sounds, that shouldn't be
a cause for concern.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.480
Director Jenkins seems to have it all figured
out, telling Deadline in May that there's

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.980
a reason why the film takes place in 1984,
which will connect to the sequel's story and

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.760
resonate with modern audiences.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.200
Jenkins explained:

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:03.620
With Wonder Woman 1984 nowhere near its June
2020 launch date and the film's promotional

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.540
cycle not kicking off until December, fans
sadly must wait a while before they can feast

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.780
their eyes on more posters and first-look
footage at the film.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.240
Hopefully the end result is worth the wait.

